1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,369
Your car makes a strange noise,

2
00:00:02,269 --> 00:00:04,631
and suddenly you need four hundred dollars

3
00:00:04,531 --> 00:00:05,439
you don't have.

4
00:00:05,719 --> 00:00:07,035
If that sounds familiar,

5
00:00:06,935 --> 00:00:07,896
you're not alone.

6
00:00:08,176 --> 00:00:10,440
In the Federal Reserve's yearly survey,

7
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:12,438
more than a third of American adults

8
00:00:12,338 --> 00:00:14,602
said they couldn't cover a four hundred

9
00:00:14,502 --> 00:00:16,045
dollar surprise with cash.

10
00:00:16,325 --> 00:00:18,468
Today I'll show you how to build

11
00:00:18,368 --> 00:00:20,512
an emergency fund, step by step,

12
00:00:20,412 --> 00:00:22,108
even on a small paycheck.

13
00:00:22,908 --> 00:00:25,913
Without savings, every surprise turns into debt.

14
00:00:26,193 --> 00:00:27,916
A flat tire, a doctor visit,

15
00:00:27,816 --> 00:00:30,002
or a missed shift goes straight onto

16
00:00:29,902 --> 00:00:30,814
a credit card.

17
00:00:31,094 --> 00:00:33,633
Then the interest makes next month even tighter.

18
00:00:33,913 --> 00:00:36,018
It's not because people are bad with

19
00:00:35,918 --> 00:00:38,357
money. It's because life is unpredictable,

20
00:00:38,257 --> 00:00:39,638
and there's no cushion.

21
00:00:39,918 --> 00:00:42,237
An emergency fund breaks that cycle.

22
00:00:42,137 --> 00:00:44,578
It's the money that stands between you

23
00:00:44,478 --> 00:00:45,379
and new debt.

24
00:00:46,179 --> 00:00:47,942
You may have heard you need three

25
00:00:47,842 --> 00:00:49,554
to six months of expenses saved.

26
00:00:49,834 --> 00:00:51,684
That's a great long term goal,

27
00:00:51,584 --> 00:00:54,193
but on a low income it can feel impossible.

28
00:00:54,473 --> 00:00:56,633
So start smaller. Your first goal is

29
00:00:56,533 --> 00:00:57,835
five hundred dollars.

30
00:00:58,115 --> 00:01:00,269
That alone covers a lot of common

31
00:01:00,169 --> 00:01:02,324
surprises, like a car repair or a

32
00:01:02,224 --> 00:01:03,382
new phone screen.

33
00:01:03,662 --> 00:01:04,624
Once you hit it,

34
00:01:04,524 --> 00:01:06,724
you can raise the goal to one thousand.

35
00:01:07,524 --> 00:01:10,441
Next, find a little money that's already slipping away.

36
00:01:10,721 --> 00:01:12,990
Look for subscriptions and apps you forgot

37
00:01:12,890 --> 00:01:13,920
you're paying for.

38
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:15,553
Check for bank fees,

39
00:01:15,453 --> 00:01:17,998
like overdraft or monthly account fees.

40
00:01:17,898 --> 00:01:20,442
Many banks offer accounts without them.

41
00:01:20,722 --> 00:01:22,964
And notice the small daily extras,

42
00:01:22,864 --> 00:01:24,792
like snacks or delivery fees.

43
00:01:25,072 --> 00:01:27,108
Even sixty dollars a month adds up

44
00:01:27,008 --> 00:01:29,556
to seven hundred and twenty dollars a year.

45
00:01:30,356 --> 00:01:32,148
Now pick an amount you can save

46
00:01:32,048 --> 00:01:34,277
every single week, no matter how small.

47
00:01:34,557 --> 00:01:36,832
Ten dollars a week becomes five hundred

48
00:01:36,732 --> 00:01:38,450
and twenty dollars in a year.

49
00:01:38,730 --> 00:01:41,680
Twenty five dollars a week becomes thirteen hundred.

50
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:45,005
And fifty dollars a week becomes twenty six hundred.

51
00:01:45,285 --> 00:01:47,711
The amount matters less than the habit.

52
00:01:47,611 --> 00:01:49,857
Consistency is what builds the fund.

53
00:01:50,657 --> 00:01:52,904
The easiest way to stay consistent is

54
00:01:52,804 --> 00:01:54,528
to take willpower out of it.

55
00:01:54,808 --> 00:01:57,201
Set up an automatic transfer to your

56
00:01:57,101 --> 00:01:58,793
emergency fund on payday.

57
00:01:59,073 --> 00:02:01,426
Many banks and credit unions let you

58
00:02:01,326 --> 00:02:03,053
split your direct deposit,

59
00:02:02,953 --> 00:02:06,558
so part of each paycheck lands in savings automatically.

60
00:02:06,838 --> 00:02:08,267
Then your bills get paid,

61
00:02:08,167 --> 00:02:09,810
and the rest is for spending.

62
00:02:10,090 --> 00:02:12,066
Money you never see in your checking

63
00:02:11,966 --> 00:02:14,463
account is money you won't accidentally spend.

64
00:02:14,743 --> 00:02:16,899
Start with whatever amount feels easy,

65
00:02:16,799 --> 00:02:19,008
and raise it a little every few months.

66
00:02:19,808 --> 00:02:21,447
Where you keep the money matters too.

67
00:02:21,727 --> 00:02:23,695
If it sits in your checking account,

68
00:02:23,595 --> 00:02:24,888
it's too easy to spend.

69
00:02:25,168 --> 00:02:27,566
Keep it in a separate savings account,

70
00:02:27,466 --> 00:02:29,320
ideally a high yield one at a

71
00:02:29,220 --> 00:02:31,678
federally insured bank or credit union.

72
00:02:31,958 --> 00:02:33,581
Some people even keep it at a

73
00:02:33,481 --> 00:02:35,735
different bank, so it's not sitting right

74
00:02:35,635 --> 00:02:37,259
next to their everyday money.

75
00:02:37,539 --> 00:02:39,904
Avoid investing your emergency fund.

76
00:02:39,804 --> 00:02:41,225
It needs to be there,

77
00:02:41,125 --> 00:02:43,616
at full value, the moment you need it.

78
00:02:44,416 --> 00:02:45,840
Want to get there faster?

79
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:48,489
Use money that isn't part of your normal paycheck.

80
00:02:48,769 --> 00:02:50,646
A tax refund, if you get one,

81
00:02:50,546 --> 00:02:53,282
can fill your starter fund in a single day.

82
00:02:53,562 --> 00:02:55,129
A few hours of side work,

83
00:02:55,029 --> 00:02:57,241
or selling things you no longer use,

84
00:02:57,141 --> 00:02:58,355
can add up quickly.

85
00:02:58,635 --> 00:03:01,089
Even cash gifts can go straight into the fund.

86
00:03:01,369 --> 00:03:03,103
Try sending at least half of any

87
00:03:03,003 --> 00:03:04,175
surprise money there.

88
00:03:04,975 --> 00:03:07,390
Decide ahead of time what counts as

89
00:03:07,290 --> 00:03:08,514
a real emergency.

90
00:03:08,794 --> 00:03:10,915
A car repair you need for work,

91
00:03:10,815 --> 00:03:13,001
a medical bill, or a sudden drop

92
00:03:12,901 --> 00:03:13,979
in income? Yes.

93
00:03:14,259 --> 00:03:15,836
A great sale, a concert,

94
00:03:15,736 --> 00:03:16,944
or a holiday trip?

95
00:03:16,844 --> 00:03:19,221
Those deserve their own savings goal.

96
00:03:19,501 --> 00:03:21,799
A simple test: is it unexpected,

97
00:03:21,699 --> 00:03:24,135
is it necessary, and is it urgent?

98
00:03:24,035 --> 00:03:26,196
If not, it's not an emergency.

99
00:03:26,476 --> 00:03:28,106
And if you do use the fund,

100
00:03:28,006 --> 00:03:30,032
that's okay. That's what it's for.

101
00:03:29,932 --> 00:03:32,015
Just start refilling it right away.

102
00:03:32,815 --> 00:03:34,285
Here's the full roadmap,

103
00:03:34,185 --> 00:03:35,427
one stage at a time.

104
00:03:35,707 --> 00:03:37,327
First, five hundred dollars.

105
00:03:37,227 --> 00:03:38,684
That's your starter fund.

106
00:03:38,964 --> 00:03:40,604
Then, one thousand dollars,

107
00:03:40,504 --> 00:03:41,801
for a bigger cushion.

108
00:03:42,081 --> 00:03:44,842
Next, three months of essential expenses,

109
00:03:44,742 --> 00:03:47,892
like rent, food, utilities, and transportation.

110
00:03:48,172 --> 00:03:49,877
And over time, if you can,

111
00:03:49,777 --> 00:03:52,036
six months. Every stage makes you a

112
00:03:51,936 --> 00:03:53,579
little safer than before.

113
00:03:54,379 --> 00:03:55,368
Let's recap.

114
00:03:55,648 --> 00:03:56,751
Start with a small,

115
00:03:56,651 --> 00:03:58,600
clear goal of five hundred dollars.

116
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:02,213
Find hidden money in fees and forgotten subscriptions.

117
00:04:02,493 --> 00:04:04,250
Save a fixed amount every week.

118
00:04:04,530 --> 00:04:06,312
Automate the transfer on payday.

119
00:04:06,592 --> 00:04:08,087
And keep it in a separate,

120
00:04:07,987 --> 00:04:09,375
insured savings account.

121
00:04:10,175 --> 00:04:11,948
You don't need a big income to

122
00:04:11,848 --> 00:04:13,008
build a safety net.

123
00:04:12,908 --> 00:04:14,290
You just need to start,

124
00:04:14,190 --> 00:04:15,127
and keep going.

125
00:04:15,407 --> 00:04:17,382
Every dollar you set aside today is

126
00:04:17,282 --> 00:04:19,900
one less dollar you'll have to borrow tomorrow.

127
00:04:20,180 --> 00:04:21,458
If this video helped,

128
00:04:21,358 --> 00:04:23,534
like it and subscribe for more simple

129
00:04:23,434 --> 00:04:25,329
ways to feel calmer about money.

130
00:04:25,609 --> 00:04:27,019
Tell me in the comments:

131
00:04:26,919 --> 00:04:28,983
how much is your first savings goal?

132
00:04:28,883 --> 00:04:30,293
See you in the next one.
